### 错误标注（序号）
1. a integral → an integral（integral 元音开头）
2. lunur → lunar（拼写错误）
3. at lunur August fifteen → on the 15th day of the lunar eighth month（农历日期固定表达，介词用 on）
4. circle → round（circle 是名词 / 动词；round 形容词：圆的）
5. in this day → on this day（具体某一天介词 on）
6. Past thousands of years → For thousands of years（固定搭配）
7. Mid-Autumn Festival take → the Mid-Autumn Festival takes（主语单数，缺定冠词，三单）
8. missing → longing（missing 是形容词；longing 名词：思念）
9. chinese → Chinese（首字母大写）
10. forwards → wishes（用词错误，wish：期盼、愿望）
11. for getting together finely → for reunion（finely 用词奇怪，reunion 为名词更地道）


### 美化原句
In China, the Mid-Autumn Festival is an important traditional festival falling on the 15th day of the lunar eighth month. The moon is round and bright on this day, symbolizing 
family reunion. When the festival arrives, family members gather to admire the moon and eat mooncakes. As the special food for the Mid-Autumn Festival, mooncakes come in a wide 
variety of flavors. For thousands of years, the Mid-Autumn Festival embodies people’s longing for their family members and carries Chinese people’s sincere wish for reunion.


### 标准参考译文
The Mid-Autumn Festival is an important traditional festival in China, falling on the 15th day of the eighth lunar month. The moon is round and bright on this day, symbolizing 
family reunion. On the festival, family members get together to admire the moon and enjoy mooncakes. Mooncakes are the special food for the Mid-Autumn Festival with diverse 
flavors. For thousands of years, the festival expresses people’s longing for their loved ones and represents Chinese people’s desire for reunion.
